ect-trajectory/scripts/adjudicate_brief.py;project-trajectory/prompts/adjudicate-first-approval.template.md;project-trajectory/prompts/adjudicate-amendment.template.md;project-trajectory/scripts/hats.py;project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3749-code_symbol = \"sitting_hat_block/round_hat_block/round_questions/fill_hat_slot/sitting_tail/hat_surface_for_work_item/NOT_A_ROUND/HAT_SLOT/HAT_PARENTS/_roster_refusal/compose/combined_values/context_from_work_item/_authoring_tags\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3750-detail = \"A sitting brief for a decomposition round carries every declared perspective question applicable to that round and asks the verdict to name one outcome for each perspective. The verdict's per-perspective outcome lines are neither row-ruling lines nor machine lines, so a verdict carrying them parses to the same rulings and judged rows as one without them. A decomposition round judges a system requirement awaiting first approval or an approved stakeholder need whose text is amended; another judged set carries no perspective question. The applicable set combines each amended need with each need named by a system requirement the sitting judges, including an amended system requirement, widens each need by the authoring work item's declared tags, and evaluates each need alone. A first-approval or amendment row a route mints records the declared tags of the work items that route names as its authors, and those tags stand in place of the row's own classification; a route naming no authoring work item records none, and the row widens by its own tags. Such a row minted from a minted row passes that record on, so the minted and in-lane sittings for one system requirement reach one perspective set wherever the authoring work item is named. Questions fill the perspective slot only when the sitting template declares it; a template without that slot composes unchanged. A sitting composed from several judgement kinds carries the questions once. Outside a decomposition round the roster is not read. An absent roster yields its no-perspective line, while an unreadable existing roster refuses a round's composition only when its template declares the perspective slot, and names the roster.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3751-rationale = \"A decomposition review needs the applicable questions in the same brief and verdict that record its judgement. Treating each parent need independently prevents tags from one sibling widening another, while an optional slot preserves briefs that do not conduct a decomposition review.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3752-test_refs = \"TC-399\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3753-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3754-component = \"CMP-008\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3755-phase = 5\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3756-\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3757-[design.LLR-361]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3758-sr_refs = [\"SR-178\"]\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3759-title = \"Act-ledger entries record the registry files an act copied\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3760-module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/baseline_snapshot.py\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3761-code_symbol = \"_record_act/parse_acts/acts_problems/_copied_problems/_copied_order_problems/added_acts_problems/added_acts_findings/record_findings\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3762-detail = \"An act-ledger entry written by a snapshot records `copied` as the non-empty sorted distinct canonical paths of the snapshot registry files that act wrote. A legacy entry has no copy set, which reads as unknown rather than empty and is not inferred. An entry a commit adds relative to each parent carries `copied` naming only snapshot registry files. An entry a commit adds relative to each parent without `copied`, or with `copied` naming a file outside the snapshot's registry files, is refused. A whole ledger refuses an entry that omits `copied` after an entry that carries it. A malformed parent or hand-edited ledger lies outside this commit-bound reading. A copied file does not establish that its rows were judged.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3763-rationale = \"Row ids identify only approvals and re-attestations, so they cannot establish every registry an act copied. Recording the copied files at the writer preserves that fact for readers without reconstructing it from mutable state, while legacy history remains readable without a false empty-set claim.\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3764-test_refs = \"TC-400\"\ndocs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml-3765-status = \"Approved\"\n--\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4042-evidence = \"tests/test_parent_first.py::test_a_commit_side_registry_that_cannot_be_read_or_does_not_parse_is_refused_by_name; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_a_diff_git_cannot_produce_is_a_refusal_not_a_skip; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_a_parent_side_that_does_not_parse_counts_every_status_as_moved; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_the_rule_rides_the_lane_commit_walk; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_the_pre_commit_hook_runs_the_parent_first_step; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_staging_an_approved_child_under_a_drafted_parent_is_refused; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_demoting_a_parent_under_an_approved_child_is_refused; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_founded_child_flipped_under_a_drafted_parent_is_refused; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_an_act_approving_parent_and_child_together_passes; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_commit_moving_neither_row_passes_over_a_standing_case; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_commit_touching_no_registry_is_not_read; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_registry_added_with_a_violation_is_refused; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_commit_repairing_an_unparseable_registry_is_judged_on_its_own_rows; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_merge_assembling_a_violation_from_two_sides_is_refused; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_merge_bringing_a_standing_case_to_the_other_side_is_refused; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_no_verify_lane_commit_with_a_violation_is_refused_at_the_slot; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_the_first_commit_is_not_judged; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_legacy_csv_carrier_is_judged_like_toml; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_an_unreadable_parent_side_counts_every_status_as_moved; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_when_both_carriers_of_a_tier_exist_the_first_listed_decides; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_lane_merge_commit_is_judged_against_every_parent; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_each_line_names_its_tree_before_the_relationship; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_parent_with_a_missing_or_unknown_status_refuses_the_commit; tests/test_parent_first_git.py::test_a_root_commit_is_not_judged; tests/test_parent_first.py::test_a_tier_absent_on_the_commit_side_supplies_no_rows\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4043-status = \"Approved\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4044-phase = 6\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4045-\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml:4046:[test.TC-399]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4047-verifies = [\"SR-161\", \"LLR-360\", \"IF-092\", \"SR-186\"]\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4048-level = \"Unit\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4049-method = \"Exercise each state of the hat block: a non-round neither reads the roster nor asks a perspective question; a first-approved system requirement or amended approved need makes the round, and every judged system requirement's need and every amended need is a parent; work-item tags widen one need without merging siblings; a minted row's recorded authoring tags stand in place of its own, and a row minted from a minted row passes them on; the minted and in-lane rows for one system requirement compose one hat set; a route naming no authoring work item leaves the row widening by its own tags; an absent roster supplies the no-perspective line; an unreadable roster refuses and names it; each applicable perspective receives one non-ruling outcome line; declared template slots receive the block while undeclared slots compose unchanged; a combined sitting carries one union block; and those outcome lines do not alter parsed row rulings or judged rows.\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4050-tier = \"Full\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4051-expected = \"Satisfies LLR-360 (parent SR-161): a decomposition-round sitting presents each applicable perspective question and requires one outcome, while another sitting has no perspective question; the minted and in-lane routes reach one perspective set for one system requirement wherever the authoring work item is named; optional-slot, combined-sitting, absent-roster, unreadable-roster, and verdict-parsing outcomes remain as stated.\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4052-automated = \"Yes\"\ndocs/test/test-cases.toml-4053-evidence = \"tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_sitting_with_no_first_approval_sr_and_no_amended_need_says_it_is_no_decomposition_round; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_outside_a_round_the_roster_is_not_read; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_an_amended_need_is_a_parent_the_work_items_refs_do_not_reach; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_judged_sr_reaches_hats_through_the_need_it_names; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_the_work_items_tags_widen_each_need_and_sibling_needs_never_merge; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_an_absent_roster_yields_the_opt_out_line_in_a_round; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_a_malformed_roster_refuses_a_round_naming_the_roster; tests/test_plan_briefs.py::test_the_round_block_asks_one_outcome_line_per_hat_in_a_non_ruling_form; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_first_approval_of_a_drafted_sr_carries_the_hat_block; tests/test_adjudicate_brief.py::test_a_first_approval_of_llr_and_tc_rows_onl